# --- Data WE generate (not committed; regenerated from the committed inputs) ---
# Only products our own pipeline can rebuild are ignored. The pySB99 database
# (pysb99/pySB99_files/*.npy/.txt/.dat, ~151M of raw tracks/spectra/atmosphere
# inputs) IS committed so pySB99 sampling and SED generation work out of the box.
# single_star_tracks.h5 (~583 MB, a versioned data file from scripts/download_data.py or
# examples/build_stochastic_database.py; not in git). The unified feedback tables
# (*_feedback.h5) ARE committed and shipped. download_data.py moves an outdated copy aside
# into database/stale_data/.
src/toddlers/database/single_star_tracks*.h5
src/toddlers/database/stale_data/
src/toddlers/interpolants/**/hdf5/
# recollapse_data_*.hdf5 etc. (rebuilt from the evolution runs)
*.hdf5

# --- Run outputs ---
evolution_output/
evolution_logs/
cloudy_output/
*.log
*.out

# --- Regenerated example outputs (the inputs/scripts are committed) ---
examples/*.png
examples/**/*.png
# ...except this illustrative figure of the unattenuated-continuum patch effect.
!examples/nebular_continuum_att_vs_unatt.png
# ...and the shipped variable-DTM STAB sanity-check figures (the .stab inputs are not shipped).
!examples/stab/dtm_validation/*.png
examples/stab/dtm_validation/*.stab
examples/stab/stab_output/
examples/stab/cloud_family_stab_output/
examples/stab/*_interp_tables/
# default interpolant cache of the STAB build
src/toddlers/stab/cache/
examples/stab/*_sed_output_*/
examples/stab/.stab_build_complete
# (grain_comparison/*.in are committed hand-crafted Cloudy inputs)

# --- Sphinx docs (autogenerated; rebuilt by `make html` / Read the Docs) ---
docs/_build/
# sphinx-apidoc output, regenerated each build by docs/conf.py
docs/api/

# --- HPC campaign work-dirs (--work-dir): generated SLURM scripts, tasks/, results/ ---
# Created wherever the campaign / examples/hpc/run_campaign_examples.sh runs (even on
# --dry-run). Pure scratch, never committed.
runs/
runs_*/

# --- Population feedback tables generated by the examples (build-on-run, not shipped) ---
# The shipped pySB99_example_*_feedback.h5, pySB99_kroupa_100 and pySB99_topheavy_100 stay
# tracked; custom populations built by example 11 do not.
src/toddlers/database/pySB99_custom_*_feedback.h5

# --- Figures written next to the validation scripts ---
examples/eep_validation/*.pdf

# full-resolution BPASS source tables fetched by scripts/download_data.py (~1.4 GB)
src/others/
